% Garment presumptions: what is taken to be so when a listing is silent.
% Each rule cites the text that says it.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the kind of *a garment* is *a kind*; undefined.
    the fabric of *a garment* is lightweight.

the knowledge base garment presumptions includes:

rule tshirt_fabric with provenance ruling NY N362034,
        confer "To be classifiable as a T-shirt, a garment must be constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or plain interlock fabric":
the fabric of a garment is lightweight
    if the kind of the garment is T-shirt.

scenario tee is:
    the kind of tee is T-shirt.
    fabrics expects answers ["the fabric of tee is lightweight"].

query fabrics is:
    the fabric of which garment is lightweight.
